<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump focused on 'what's important to him': 'Tone-deaf for a normally shrewd populist operator'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2ce074ef7df18f152ab96b364e8fbd7c92bba1f1f4ca08a3dc29b214cbbe6c2</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:05:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator--19609ba997e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Doug Heye, Republican strategist, founder of Douglas Media, and former Communications Director for the Republican National Committee (RNC). As Americans head to the polls, Republicans face a challenge that goes beyond the familiar electoral backlash against an incumbent president. For Heye, Donald Trump's greatest political vulnerability may lie in the widening gap between his rhetoric of economic success and voters' everyday financial anxieties. "For a lot of voters, they see him focused on what's important to him, not what's important to them," Heye explains. Yet he also cautions against interpreting Democratic gains as a sign of renewed confidence in the opposition. Rather than a resurgence of partisan enthusiasm, the elections may expose an electorate increasingly disillusioned with both parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump cuts Israeli military aid: $3.8 billion in security assistance slashed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d0caa37ea8176003a4548fd476be2dbece7acb40b0e223afde7c6e1f7eaaf89</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:01:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-trump-cuts-israeli-military-aid-3-8-billion-in-security-assistance-slashed--9e8be08da6ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-trump-cuts-israeli-military-aid-3-8-billion-in-security-assistance-slashed" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, November 3, said he made a deal with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu for Washington to stop providing $3.8 billion in funding to Israel after the end of this year. FRANCE 24's Jerusalem correspondent, Noga Tarnopolsky, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Michigan Senate candidate El-Sayed becomes Democrats' rising star</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25ac1b87ac97769c8536cceed7e4df5c67679efccd00c3f214723c5c0d5a9731</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:41:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star--b86026836402.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, Democrat Abdul El-Sayed and Republican Mike Rogers are testing two sharply different strategies to win over voters in one of the nation's premier swing states on Tuesday, November 3, in a closely watched race that could determine control of the Senate. Progressive candidate El-Sayed has so far outpolled his Republican rival and is emerging as one of the Democratic Party's rising stars.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Michigan candidate El-Sayed pledges to tackle the affordability crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81f7c1d04a3d86058fad4e36781d05d4bb19b5789c348e618591f8340900d1b4</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:34:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis--9ec59f3a2e71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis" /><summary type="html">The cost of living is one of the main concerns for many US voters as the midterm elections get underway. In Michigan, Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed has pledged to "take the money out of politics and put it in your pocket", as FRANCE 24 correspondent Jessica Le Masurier reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>A cultural stroll through Paris with actors François-Xavier Demaison and François Morel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2fc4d44999fa581ceb749bb17fac93e788287ef18ceed03f9c275f7d72b1df8</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:30:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/paris-des-arts/20261103-a-cultural-stroll-through-paris-with-actors-fran_ois-xavier-demaison-and-fran_ois-morel--6a2d65016129.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/paris-des-arts/20261103-a-cultural-stroll-through-paris-with-actors-fran%C3%A7ois-xavier-demaison-and-fran%C3%A7ois-morel" /><summary type="html">This week, we bring you a special programme dedicated to theatre. Valérie Fayolle takes us to the Renaissance Theatre, where François-Xavier Demaison takes us behind the scenes of "Laponie". The fiesty comedy shows how a family's holiday gathering can quickly turn into a settling of scores. "Theatre is one of our last collective experiences. It's magnificent, we're in a bubble," he tells us.</summary><category term="Paris des arts" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles says he has greater understanding of 'horrors' of slavery, falls short of apology</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:729e39540b3784725d4e1a9d728d845ed4b0bdb82d93bf35cc3fd43534a8c88a</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:26:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology--ae418e66f435.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-king-charles-says-he-has-greater-understanding-of-horrors-of-slavery-falls-short-of-apology" /><summary type="html">King Charles III told the heads of 56 Commonwealth countries on Tuesday that he has a greater understanding of the horrors of slavery, calling it a "shameful chapter of history". This comes as Prime Minister Andy Burnham said he was open to the United Kingdom apologising for the transatlantic slave trade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Your donut, your vote': Texas group uses free food to attract young voters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:879b73919139c5b2ff09a0f5df5806cdccd5bc402cc0b2a7e8b7bb63a46c1c40</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:26:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters--cd3ced7b6ae1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters" /><summary type="html">US voters on Tuesday headed to the polls in midterm elections that could shape the political future of the country. But navigating the voting process can sometimes discourage voters – particularly younger ones. In Texas, an organisation reached out to them directly by handing out free food, to then help them overcome these obstacles. FRANCE 24's Special envoy Tarek Kai reports from Austin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Political parallels in France and the US: Anger at the ballot box and in the streets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c99a013b920bfdd0dac5c7326899e3b24227172c5455fbf6c404dd7a335c4c5</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:21:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets--cb3c566a3efc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets" /><summary type="html">Anger has long been a driving force for political change, but with the midterm elections in the US and the ongoing protests in France, widespread anger in both nations is currently front and centre. We take a look at some of the common issues causing this anger on both sides of the Atlantic, including the rising cost of living, a loss of faith in institutions and an eroding of the social contract.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: All eyes on crucial Michigan Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86dc5d32e0a2cb71f39209151a31a5b8ee454e9d9548bf0ba791fd2959e92b4e</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race--7781aa8be6b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, the Senate race in Michigan has been one of the most closely watched in the country. It took an unexpected turn on Sunday after Democratic Congresswoman Haley Stevens endorsed Republican Mike Rogers over Democratic nominee Abdul El-Sayed. Both candidates made their final pitches to voters during campaign rallies on Monday evening, November 2. FRANCE 24's Jessica Le Masurier reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says US will halt $4 billion in aid to Israel after end of the year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17fda8bb2ccac7d54d18fe12e5897fc2a0ea21f9cf2dcc8abfff13e58c3870fb</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:35:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-trump-says-us-will-halt-4-billion-in-aid-to-israel-after-end-of-this-year--ad88efbaf029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-trump-says-us-will-halt-4-billion-in-aid-to-israel-after-end-of-this-year" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Tuesday said that the United States will stop $4 billion in funding to Israel after the end of this year. While speaking to Fox News' Fox and Friends, the US president added that Israel no longer needed the aid from Washington, and that some politicians were using the funding to criticise Republicans.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Prix Goncourt: France's prestigious literary prize awarded to Philippe Jaenada</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29f228b02652f6a6df5f58f52662ba558d83b5701ecbd5882c5d9b50e6a670de</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:21:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-2026-prix-goncourt-france-s-prestigious-literary-prize-awarded-to-philippe-jaenada--0c04b5f54d4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-2026-prix-goncourt-france-s-prestigious-literary-prize-awarded-to-philippe-jaenada" /><summary type="html">France’s prestigious literary prize “The Goncourt” was awarded on Monday to writer Philippe Jaenada. The prize carries a symbolic reward of only 10 euros, but results in considerable recognition and book sales for the winning author. FRANCE 24’s Culture reporter Olivia Salazar-Winspear reports from the Parisian restaurant where the jury made the call.</summary></entry><entry><title>Americans vote in key midterms set to upend Trump presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16fa72abefbaf57e4dbe3fa5a1484b055401f8d243bf7956711d3b75c65f1b0a</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-americans-vote-in-key-midterms-set-to-upend-trump-presidency--17e7797a3acd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-americans-vote-in-key-midterms-set-to-upend-trump-presidency" /><summary type="html">Americans voted on Tuesday in pivotal midterm elections with Democrats hoping to seize control of Congress and impose the first significant checks on Donald Trump's chaotic second term in the White House. Republicans losing the House would give Democrats the power to stall Trump's legislative agenda and launch sweeping investigations of his administration. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington, DC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli opposition leaders vow to remove Netanyahu quickly but path unclear</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d97446f63c57848dd5ef2c124f80d70a986177042ce1b4a963b1729c6c36a0b2</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-israeli-opposition-leaders-vow-to-remove-netanyahu-quickly-but-path-unclear--91e481e62a13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-israeli-opposition-leaders-vow-to-remove-netanyahu-quickly-but-path-unclear" /><summary type="html">The Israeli opposition bloc led by Gadi Eisenkot pledged Tuesday to form a government quickly to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu but remained unclear on how, with divisions over whether to ally with Arab lawmakers. Arab-majority parties last week won 19 seats in the 120-member parliament. Eisenkot's diverse opposition bloc won 48 seats while Netanyahu's camp secured 53, of which 27 are from his Likud party.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: A referendum on President Donald Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf7f5a8a45f13efdafda228ec42d65d1343c262913787b6bc886ae60023b5891</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-a-referendum-on-president-donald-trump--406ec9ab4507.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-a-referendum-on-president-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Americans deliver their verdict on Donald Trump's tumultuous first term in midterm elections that threaten to shatter his grip on Washington, with Democrats poised to seize the House and within striking distance of the Senate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Californians vote on ballot initiative to impose one-time tax on billionaires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e77e069ee296c32942d8749199faba1323aeb51ce29c8e1ede85c707d577a93</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:51:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261103-californians-vote-on-ballot-initiative-to-impose-one-time-tax-on-billionaires--26dcd70a0e65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261103-californians-vote-on-ballot-initiative-to-impose-one-time-tax-on-billionaires" /><summary type="html">This Tuesday, Californians are voting on a landmark plan to impose a one-time tax on billionaires to fund the state's healthcare system. We take a closer look. Also on the show: global oil prices fell sharply on the eve of the US midterm elections. This came after Iran said it was holding intensive talks through mediators towards negotiating peace and signalled that it was ready to reopen the Strait of Hormuz if the US accepted its conditions. Both Brent and WTI fell by around 8 percent.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Poland foils attempted 'provocation' on Russian border, PM Tusk says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce873de736879a0349c27a75ae499ed2e4a556536c6c3743c99ef5d8087e1214</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:39:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-poland-prevented-attempted-provocation-russian-border-pm-tusk-says--aab9903dd48c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261103-poland-prevented-attempted-provocation-russian-border-pm-tusk-says" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Donald Tusk said Tuesday that Poland prevented an attempted "provocation" on its border with the Russian exclave of Kaliningrad overnight. He gave few details but said Polish security forces prevented any incident from happening.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme court rejects Trump request to set aside 20,000 California ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccad7abc3ebe2882204b2dda50cc47dfc0c2ae1fa898f3511d6a52579b2b32d1</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:27:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-request-to-set-aside-20-000-california-ballots--ad9a6e802fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-request-to-set-aside-20-000-california-ballots" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court rejected the Trump administration’s push to force California to set aside 20,000 ballots from people the federal government claims are noncitizens, a decision that came hours before the final day of voting in the pivotal midterm elections. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>What could happen if Donald Trump loses US midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19556c5479f5f98e94f1abae2f8f77a65e76c1a8c0fb5aa8f880f44be6d8e6a0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:24:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-what-could-happen-if-donald-trump-loses-us-midterm-elections--9795768d7bcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-what-could-happen-if-donald-trump-loses-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Americans head to the polls on Tuesday in pivotal midterm elections, with Democrats hoping to seize control of Congress and impose the first significant checks on Donald Trump's second term in the White House. But what could happen in the United States if Republicans lose control of Congress? FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'I love giving debut novelists a chance': Shakespeare and Company's Adam Biles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c77c308ba02184cb99f75af1cb41f2f74744c00981daa4435a8b693a515e8c06</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:24:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261103-i-love-giving-debut-novelists-a-chance-shakespeare-and-company-s-adam-biles--d90efc8624c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261103-i-love-giving-debut-novelists-a-chance-shakespeare-and-company-s-adam-biles" /><summary type="html">The literary director of the English-language Paris bookshop Shakespeare and Company says that the shop has achieved such notoriety that invitations to authors to appear there are usually accepted. Adam Biles says the shop enjoys inviting both famous authors to speak there, as well as debut authors who deserve the exposure. Adam hosts the events himself, and over the years has interviewed hundreds of different literary figures of varying notoriety. Many of the shop's guests speak to us in Perspective before or after their appearances. We spoke to Adam in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Could a blue wave widen the centrist-progressive divide among Democrats ahead of 2028?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28638be3d053ea6e304b82ddb35cba64e851d66a3e4287ec8156753cb1de2214</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:22:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:19:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-could-a-blue-wave-widen-the-centrist-progressive-divide-among-democrats-ahead-of-2028" /><summary type="html">As the US approaches the midterms, the contest is emerging as a referendum on Donald Trump, the resilience of American democratic institutions and the ability of a divided Democratic Party to transform widespread public dissatisfaction into a coherent political alternative. With some Republicans now seeking to distance themselves from Trump, Katy Hull, Assistant Professor of American Studies at the University of Amsterdam, suggests that the president's highly populist and personalised approach to politics is becoming an electoral liability. Philip Turle observes Republican voters turning towards the opposition "as a form of protest against Donald Trump", rather than an endorsement of the Democrats.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Senegal's opposition-dominated parliament rejects key revised budget bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b23cd354509e6414b933b8dd4cda98aa64363dbf9592512a9101d26901138352</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:43:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill--942d392c755d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's opposition-dominated parliament rejects revised budget bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fb7b3f67d47972e628a727c34912dd7f9f793fc22f1c61a1273b2ea7dd819e1</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:40:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill--942d392c755d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill" /><summary type="html">Senegal's powerful opposition party Pastef led by former presidential candidate Ousmane Sonko on Tuesday rejected a revised version of the country's budget, leaving the west African nation's new bailout programme with the International Monetary Fund hanging in the balance.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>US strikes Iran's Qeshm Island as midterm elections start</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:706f82b370f113921271c78869b475fb30908686346c0d4f7147c5a34a600941</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-strikes-iran-s-qeshm-island-as-midterm-elections-start--40705a7ad889.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-strikes-iran-s-qeshm-island-as-midterm-elections-start" /><summary type="html">The United States has conducted defensive strikes on some Iranian targets in the Strait of Hormuz, a US official said Monday, on the eve of crucial midterm elections. The unpopular Iran war and the resulting impact on U.S. gasoline prices and other parts of the economy have been a vulnerability for Republicans as they try to keep control of Congress. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Oliver Farry has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>French schools blockade resume on smaller scale as holidays end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77d3edce9ed574ea3bf7d7ac181b88c8c5dd5597e9d000214203395e05a56dfe</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:01:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-french-schools-blockade-resume-on-smaller-scale-as-holidays-end--e0c3a170632d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-french-schools-blockade-resume-on-smaller-scale-as-holidays-end" /><summary type="html">Students blockaded dozens of high schools across France on Tuesday to maintain pressure on the government over education reforms as trade unions prepared for a nationwide strike later this week. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry></feed>
